{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player","id":1007944,"title":"Helping my non-mage player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-24T21:53:26-08:00","id":1007944,"title":"Helping my non-mage player","content":"So i just started up my first awakening 2e game, in fact my first NWod game in years and the first time with this group. i have 3 (likely 4 soon) players and two of them are quite happy with their characters, the setting and their magical powers, easily getting into it. One player however; while she enjoys the setting and the plot, does not enjoy being a Mage. She finds the magic system a convoluted headache that left her afraid to do anything all game and the magic itself overly full of spells. i don't blame her as assigning reach, sorting out spell bonuses and penalties and even PICKING your spell can be quite the hassle. In short she wants to keep playing mage she just doesn't want to BE a mage.<br /> <br /> Now this leaves me with a bit of a problem as i don't know what to have her play that she'd enjoy. My first thought was to let her play a sleepwalker who was aiding the cabal but the problem is she enjoys punching things, solving her problems with violence and generally being a badass, and i'm uncertain she'll be happy once the group starts leaving her behind in terms of power, martial arts and a shotgun can only go so far and batman levels of strategy just isn't her style. My second thought was to let her play a proximi, perhaps with some bonus merits at creation, so she can have the powers she wants without being buried in them, but i realized she'd still need to understand and use the magic system she's already expressed dislike of, so i'd prefer another option.<br /> <br /> Now the best solution for her would be to pull up requiem or forsaken and let her player a Gangrel or a Rahu which i know she'd enjoy. the problem is i wasn't really planning on incorporating either world into the mage game, i was thinking of maybe throwing in a couple of vampires in as a one off and i wasn't planning to use werewolf at all. vampires would have alot of problems going to many of the places the cabal went, both due to a lack of otherworld based magic and that pressing sunlight allergy, and the werewolf would cause the shadow to somewhat dominate a game that was only minorly shadow based (particularly annoying in that she was the only one who even had Spirit and even then only 1 dot, so the other player would be SoL), and i had no intention of bringing in the tribes or auspices.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping i'd be able to find a minor template that i might tweak a bit but i'm not seeing one that wouldn't be a whole lot of work. does anyone know a good solution to the problem i'm facing right now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:22:21-08:00","id":1007949,"title":"","content":"Beast is pretty mechanically straightforward \u2014 it's explicitly designed to be crossover-friendly, none of the powers are scaled, the characters have precious non-Yantra bonus dice to offer as a teamwork aid, its primary otherworld is an obscure corner of one that no other game but Mage presently deals with, and the way its Integrity equivalent works can help keep up with the gains Arcane Experience represents.<br /> <br /> Character creation might take a bit of sorting out, given how front-loaded some aspects of it are, but if her primary issues with Awakened spellcasting are the breadth of examples and variable overload, Beast lends itself fairly well to &quot;punch things good&quot; as a problem-solving tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:29:20-08:00","id":1007950,"title":"","content":"Loading her up on Supernatural Merits, which can only be taken by mortals anyway, looks promising.<br /> <br /> Or you could just use the mechanics for, say, vampiric Disciplines or werewolf Gifts for her powers without saying that they actually are those same powers.<br /> <br /> For example, maybe the character has Super Strength, Super Stamina, and Super Speed. Within the game world, people say that her body is infused with Supernal energies, making her a subtype of Proximi whose Blessings are her supreme physical prowess instead of sorcery. However, on the character sheet, you give her dots in Vigor, Resilience, and Celerity from Vampire, using its effects while replacing the Vitae cost with either Willpower or Mana as you see fit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T23:22:22-08:00","id":1007960,"title":"","content":"Remember that <i>any</i> character with Supernatural Powers/Merits is treated as Sleepwalker for Supernal Magic. So your non-mage player can easily have any Supernatural Merits she wants, in any configuration. Most of those from 1E <b>Second Sight</b> book are updated in 2E <b>CoD Rulebook</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If she will change her mind on proper<b> Mage</b> mechanics, you can easily Awaken her later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> mentioned, you can say she was infused with Supernal Energies. Or just she is result of other weird phenomena, full in World of (Chronicles) of Darkness - and by this - she is living Mystery on it self and by this great source of Obsession for two other proper mage players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would then advise to give 1 extra Obsession slot for mage players, to have them 'for free' non-mage player character as common Obsession. I done the same thing in my <b>Mage/Promethean</b> crossover game - my Awakened players are all Obsessed over our Created character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-25-2016, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:18:32-08:00","id":1007999,"title":"","content":"I had a similar problem with one of my players, and succesfully solved it by leting her to play a powered up Thyrsus related Proximi. Thyrsus because non of the players followed this path. I Gave her character more trait dots, some nice blessings (spells) ans she can do some nice contributions to the cabal. Just simplify her blessings fixing spell factors and letting her to roll a fixed pool, is not in the rules but I'm sure the Brookshaw's Corps Intervention Unit will not interrupt your game for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:33:51-08:00","id":1008001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player?p=1007949#post1007949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is pretty mechanically straightforward \u2014 it's explicitly designed to be crossover-friendly, none of the powers are scaled, the characters have precious non-Yantra bonus dice to offer as a teamwork aid, its primary otherworld is an obscure corner of one that no other game but Mage presently deals with, and the way its Integrity equivalent works can help keep up with the gains Arcane Experience represents.<br /> <br /> Character creation might take a bit of sorting out, given how front-loaded some aspects of it are, but if her primary issues with Awakened spellcasting are the breadth of examples and variable overload, Beast lends itself fairly well to &quot;punch things good&quot; as a problem-solving tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Also, I think Beasts (and other splats) count as Sleepwalkers for the various benefits that gives, including being able to hold spells for the cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T03:14:07-08:00","id":1008011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player#post1007944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...i wasn't planning to use werewolf at all. vampires would have alot of problems going to many of the places the cabal went, both due to a lack of otherworld based magic and that pressing sunlight allergy...</div> </div> </div> </div>If she is the punching style, but playing a vampire is a problem, you can let her play a Ghoul with dots in Vigor, Resilience and Celerity. Easy to use powers and less crunch... and an interesting plot. Why is a Vampire lending his/her ghoul to the players...?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think that letting her play a werewolf will make the Shadow take a strong presence. A Rahu from the Masters of Iron, whose prey are Humans of all kind (mortal and supernatural), is less Shadow-centered as, for example, an Ithaeur Bone Shadow.<br /> <br /> If the rules for werewolves are also crunchy for her, go for the Ghoul or a mortal with supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T03:42:31-08:00","id":1008017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player?p=1008001#post1008001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding this. Also, I think Beasts (and other splats) count as Sleepwalkers for the various benefits that gives, including being able to hold spells for the cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too vote for a Beast character, but for hold a spell a p(n)c must have an Integrity score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:00:05-08:00","id":1008044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player?p=1008017#post1008017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I too vote for a Beast character, but for hold a spell a p(n)c must have an Integrity score.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepwalker (\u2022) <b>Prerequisite</b>: Integrity<br /> With this Merit, your character is considered a Sleepwalker. <b>Effect: </b>The character is immune to the Curse, causes no Dissonance, and follows the other guidelines for Sleepwalkers in this section. <b>This Merit is not necessary for a character with any other Supernatural Merit involving an internal power, or any supernatural template. </b> </div> </div> </div>I take the above to mean that any supernatural template counts as being a Sleepwalker for all purposes, including holding spells. As far as I know, that's not directly contradicted anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:15:55-08:00","id":1008049,"title":"","content":"I had a player like this in one of my 1E campaigns, opted to play an Obrimos with Forces/Life magic. The spells in those arcana are really easy to apply and know when then they'd be useful. It was great because he originally started off just using the spells for the obvious stuff (direct damage + healing) but as he became more comfortable with the system he started to branch out in all the other applications of the arcana. <br /> <br /> I was also a part of a group like this once where a player played a character from Hunter, which would require some work on your part to convert to 2E. But their abilities are much narrower and easier to apply in real time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:56:28-08:00","id":1008064,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have a player who's brand new and playing an Obrimos. He started out not really knowing when to use magic or how so he avoided doing so. After a few situations where magic simply was the most obvious, easiest route and a bit of explanation from an NPC he's gotten better.<br /> <br /> Since this seems to be a problem with grasping the mechanical complexities though something like Beast might be easier to enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:26:35-08:00","id":1008075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007944-helping-my-non-mage-player?p=1008044#post1008044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I take the above to mean that any supernatural template counts as being a Sleepwalker for all purposes, including holding spells. As far as I know, that's not directly contradicted anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I re read it: agree with you !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:54:05-08:00","id":1008084,"title":"","content":"As much as I dislike the directionlessness of Beast, I have to join in and say that this is the perfect place to add one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:02:56-08:00","id":1008401,"title":"","content":"I would let her write up the werewolf butt kicker you know she would enjoy and then adjust my chronicle to include however much of the Shadow and Spirits she showed interest in. As already mentioned having a werewolf in the group doesn't require the Shadow to be that important, besides if her character is the only one capable of dealing with such it just provides her opportunities to release her inner snowflake.<br /> \u200bAs long as everyone at the table enjoys the game...you win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:50:17-08:00","id":1010162,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Werewolf, but you might want to consider a Changeling (Troll) as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:55:23-08:00","id":1010266,"title":"","content":"I'll throw in for beast as well. This is pretty much the nitch it was designed for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:16:09-08:00","id":1011749,"title":"","content":"I suggest you to tweak a Major Template instead of a Minor one. It isn't as hard as it seems.<br /> <br /> A lot of mechanics in Major Templates are distinct and present for the sake of theme, not of balance, and the entirety of the theme and setting can be taken out if it doesn't interfere with your particular chronicle.<br /> <br /> Lets see a vampire, as an example. Weakness to Sunlight and most rules on Torpor, Frenzy and Humanity don't balance the game in any way. The first just make Vampire games happen at night, the other serve to set theme. Get rid of all four, and the character won't be an inch stronger for a Mage game, but will be far less of a hassle. The weakness to Fire, on the other hand, is effective in play, but still optional. The Mages are going to take care of that anyway, sooner than later. Most of the core mechanics are simple to use, and then you simply discard unneeded adds. You can do essentially this to any Major Template, so Vampire can make for a fast and effective option (get out all the curses and Banes stuff, anything you really need Humanity for you default it to 7). Werewolf does need the rules for Frenzy after too much time on Gauru, but that's about it. And so forth.<br /> <br /> Then you let the player construct her own explanation to be as she is IC. She can be an experiment, a failed Awakening, a Supernal Being trapped in the Lie, an exceptional Proximi that somehow became an embodiment of a forgotten Legacy, or even a weird case of a Tamed Abyssal Intrusion (chaos can, after all, produce anything, even order).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}